<%# A photograph printed in the site's two inks: shadows in bottle green, light in
    cream. The only way a photograph appears on the site, and at most one per
    view. Sources and licences: docs/redesign/IMAGE_CREDITS.md.
    Locals:
      src    (String) asset path of a greyscale image under app/assets/images
      alt    (String) what the photograph shows
      css    (String, optional) sizing classes, e.g. an aspect ratio
      width, height (Integer, optional) the file's pixel size, so the
             browser reserves the space before the lazy image arrives
    Motion (the appear controller): the photograph settles from a slight
    scale to its place the first time it is seen (photo), clipped by the
    frame so nothing shifts, and fades in if it is still loading (image). %>
<figure class="duotone <%= local_assigns[:css] %>" data-appear-target="photo">
  <%= image_tag src, alt: alt, loading: "lazy", decoding: "async", width: local_assigns[:width], height: local_assigns[:height], data: { appear_target: "image" } %>
</figure>
